SynthSeg

Labelling in Volsa (the volsa-segment crate) is a port to Rust of SynthSeg's own
code: the steps of predict_synthseg.py that prepare a scan for SynthSeg's
networks, take the steps between them and tidy their answer into labels, and
the lab2im functions those steps call.

    SynthSeg
    Copyright 2020 Benjamin Billot
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (a copy is in
    LICENSE-APACHE).
    https://github.com/BBillot/SynthSeg

Volsa's port changes SynthSeg as docs/models.md (MODELS.md in a download of
Volsa) describes under "What Volsa does differently from SynthSeg's own
program": a part's volume is counted in voxels, where SynthSeg adds up
probabilities; the scan may be cut to the head when memory is short; and the
cortex network's answer is reduced to areas inside the file.

SynthSeg's trained networks are not part of Volsa and do not come with it.
SynthSeg's authors ask that work which uses it cite one of the SynthSeg
papers, listed at the address above.
